.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 30, 2026
.Dt NQKSTMT 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqkstmt ,
.Nm nqkexp
.Nd make a key statement: a rotation, a revocation or an expiry
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft int
.Fo nqkstmt
.Fa "nqsalg alg" "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *pk" "size_t pklen"
.Fa "nqsalg nalg" "const uint8_t *nsk" "size_t nsklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *npk" "size_t npklen"
.Fa "int64_t at" "const char *reason"
.Fa "char *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqkexp
.Fa "nqsalg alg" "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *pk" "size_t pklen"
.Fa "int64_t at" "const char *reason"
.Fa "char *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nqkstmt
writes to
.Fa out ,
of
.Fa cap
bytes, a key statement
.Pq Ql noqtis-keys-1 , Xr noqtis-capsule 5
in canonical JSON.
With
.Fa nsk
and
.Fa npk
given, it is a rotation: the holder of the key pair
.Fa sk , pk
of
.Fa alg
says that from time
.Fa at
(seconds since 1970-01-01T00:00:00Z) it is replaced by
.Fa nsk , npk
of
.Fa nalg ,
and both keys sign it.
With
.Fa nsk
and
.Fa npk
.Dv NULL ,
it is a revocation of
.Fa pk
from
.Fa at ,
signed by it.
.Fa reason
is
.Dv NULL
or up to 255 bytes of UTF-8 with no control character.
.Fa *outlen
gets the statement's size, also when
.Fa cap
is too small.
.Fa reason
.Dv NULL
is stored as the empty string.
.Pp
In symbols, with B64 the padded base64 of RFC 4648 section 4, ALG and
NALG the algorithms' names as
.Xr nqsign 3
gives them, T the time
.Fa at
as
.Ql YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ ,
KIND
.Ql rotate ,
.Ql revoke
or
.Ql expire ,
and JCS the canonical JSON of RFC 8785:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
body = JCS({"alg": ALG, "at": T, "format": "noqtis-keys-1",
            "key": B64(pk), "kind": KIND,
            "new_alg": NALG, "new_key": B64(npk),     rotation only
            "reason": reason})
sig     = Sign(sk, body, "noqtis-keys-1")
new_sig = Sign(nsk, body, "noqtis-keys-1")             rotation only
stmt = JCS(body's members, "new_signature": B64(new_sig),
           "signature": B64(sig))
.Ed
.Pp
where Sign is
.Xr nqsign 3 ,
pure and hedged, with the 13-byte context
.Ql noqtis-keys-1 :
both keys of a rotation sign the same body.
.Pp
Each signature is verified before the statement is written.
.Xr nqchkx 3
follows statements from a trusted key through its
.Fa stmt
option.
.Pp
.Fn nqkexp
writes a statement of the kind
.Ql expire :
the key pair
.Fa sk , pk
seals until
.Fa at
and not after.
Until then a check with the statement accepts its seals as it does
without one; from then on, by the system clock
.Po Ev SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH ,
which sets only the times noqtis writes, does not change it
.Pc ,
it accepts only a seal with a
verified timestamp from before
.Fa at ,
as for a key revoked at
.Fa at .
Its limits and results are those of
.Fn nqkstmt .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Bl -tag -width NQENOSUP
.It Dv NQOK
The statement was written.
.It Bq Er NQEBUF
.Fa cap
is too small.
.It Bq Er NQENOSUP
An algorithm is not a post-quantum signature (Ed25519 alone) or not a
signature algorithm of noqtis.
.It Bq Er NQEARG
A
.Dv NULL
argument, keys of the wrong sizes or not a pair, the new key equal to
the old one (the same algorithm and the same bytes),
.Fa nsk
without
.Fa npk
or
.Fa npk
without
.Fa nsk ,
.Fa at
before 1970 or after 9999, or a reason that is too long or not plain
text.
.It Bq Er NQEMEM
The allocation hook returned
.Dv NULL .
.It Bq Er NQERNG , NQEFLT
As
.Xr nqsign 3 .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Revoke an ML-DSA-65 key from now on:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static char st[16384];
size_t n;
int rc = nqkstmt(NQMLDSA65, sk, sklen, pk, pklen, NQMLDSA65, NULL, 0,
                 NULL, 0, (int64_t)time(NULL), "key lost", st,
                 sizeof st, &n);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-revoke 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-rotate 1 ,
.Xr nqchkx 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%A A. Rundgren
.%A B. Jordan
.%A S. Erdtman
.%T JSON Canonicalization Scheme (JCS)
.%R RFC 8785
.%D June 2020
.Re
.Rs
.%T FIPS 204: Module-Lattice-Based Digital Signature Standard
.%Q NIST
.%D August 2024
.Re
.Rs
.%T FIPS 205: Stateless Hash-Based Digital Signature Standard
.%Q NIST
.%D August 2024
.Re
